  "body": "The maintainer asked for this in chat on 2026-11-15. His words: \"add the logo to the camcraft documentation. It should sit at the first page centered above the title \"CamCraft\" the square images should have had its corners rounded with CSS.\"\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Show the CamCraft logo on the first page of the documentation site (`site/`, template `site/templates/index.html`, content `site/content/_index.md`).\n2. Put the logo above the title \"CamCraft\". Center it horizontally.\n3. The logo image is square. Round its corners with CSS (`border-radius`). Do not edit the image file to round it.\n4. Use the logo of the repository (`assets/logo/camcraft-logo.png` or a size from `assets/logo/icons/`). The site build must get the file from one source: copy it at build time or keep one copy in `site/static/`, and say which in the PR.\n5. Give the image an `alt` text and a fixed display size, so that the page does not move while the image loads.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The first page of the site shows the logo, centered, above the title \"CamCraft\".\n- The corners of the logo are round, and the rule is in the site CSS.\n- `zola build` in `site/` is clean, and the site tests in `site/tests/` pass.\n- The PR body has a screenshot of the first page.\n",
